       Q: Maximising resource_efficiency has no upper saturation point: the optimiser may raise machine_speed and energy draw by 30–40% to squeeze marginal efficiency gains while still staying inside the fatigue and noise ceilings — is there an acceptable maximum energy budget (e.g. ≤ 110% of shift baseline kWh) or a minimum acceptable efficiency gain (e.g. +5% over baseline) beyond which further optimisation is not required?
