  [Escalation] Remediation options presented to manager:
    - Option 1 — Add Temporary Supplemental Shifts (Preferred): Introduce one additional shift slot per day (e.g., a short Saturday or split-shift overlay) using existing trained personnel on a voluntary-overtime or contractor basis. This adds raw capacity without changing any per-worker constraint limits, preserving all human-centric protections. Estimated to recover 15–20% of the demand gap; remaining 5–10% may be addressed through minor scheduling optimisation.
      Preserves human constraints: Yes
    - Option 2 — Approve Controlled Overtime with Enhanced Monitoring: Authorise a temporary, audited increase in maximum daily working hours (e.g., from 8 h to 10 h) for a defined cohort of volunteers for no more than two consecutive weeks. A fatigue-monitoring check-in must be conducted at the midpoint. This directly relaxes the shift-duration constraint but keeps all other human-centric limits (rest intervals, ergonomic load caps) intact. Management must log the authorisation formally for compliance purposes.
