    - Option 3 — Negotiate Phased Demand Fulfilment with Customer: Engage the customer or downstream planner to defer 20–25% of the incremental demand to the next planning horizon. This eliminates the constraint conflict entirely without relaxing any human-protective rule or stressing the workforce. It is the lowest operational risk option but depends on external agreement. Recommended when lead-time flexibility exists or when the demand spike is transient (e.g., a one-time order rather than a structural shift).
