       A: Both an instantaneous 1-minute LAeq peak limit of 80 dB and the shift-average LAeq limit of 80 dB are enforced simultaneously; whichever is more restrictive governs, consistent with conservative interpretation of EN ISO 9612 and OSHA 29 CFR 1910.95.
    5. context / delivered_value definition
       Q: Delivered value is defined as 'quality-adjusted throughput OR revenue-equivalent units' — these can diverge significantly when the product mix includes both high-margin, slow-cycle items and low-margin, fast-cycle items; which definition should the optimizer use, and is there a minimum quality acceptance rate (e.g., first-pass yield ≥ 95%) that must be satisfied before value is counted?
