    4. context.planning_horizon (shift duration)
       Q: The contract scope is 'single_shift' but no shift length is given — is this an 8-hour, 10-hour, or 12-hour shift? The fatigue accumulation model and the OSHA time-weighted average noise exposure window both depend on total shift duration, and a 12-hour shift may make the fatigue ≤ 0.4 limit infeasible at normal cycle rates.
       A: Shift duration assumed to be 8 hours; fatigue accumulation and dBA time-weighted average calculated over an 8-hour exposure window consistent with OSHA 29 CFR 1910.95.
    5. resource_efficiency vs. minimum absolute throughput floor
       Q: A high efficiency ratio can be achieved by producing very few units near-perfectly (e.g., one unit per hour with minimal waste) — is there a minimum delivered-output volume the shift must meet regardless of efficiency gains (e.g., at least 80% of the site's standard daily shift target)?
