       Q: OSHA time-weighted noise exposure limits (e.g., 85 dB(A) for 8 h vs. 82 dB(A) for 12 h) and fatigue accumulation rates both depend on shift length — is this a standard 8-hour shift, a 10-hour extended shift, or a 12-hour rotating shift?
