    4. assumptions.resource_scope (normalization weights)
       Q: Resource consumption aggregates labor-hours, energy (kWh), and material input into a single unit — what cost or utilization weights should be used (e.g., 1 labor-hour = $35, 1 kWh = $0.12, 1 kg material = $8), and if energy cost drops mid-shift, should the weights be updated dynamically or fixed at shift-start?
       A: Weights are fixed at shift-start using the plant's standard cost rates from the most recent period close. If no standard rates are available, weights default to equal normalized contribution (each resource type scaled to [0,1] by its historical shift maximum) and are held constant for the duration of the shift.
    5. operator_fatigue (dual role: KPI minimize + hard constraint ≤ 0.4)
       Q: Fatigue appears both as a hard constraint (≤ 0.4 per individual operator) and as a soft KPI to minimize — if the fleet average fatigue is 0.18 but one operator is at 0.39, is the constraint satisfied and should the optimiser continue pushing efficiency upward, or should individual operators near the 0.4 ceiling trigger a rebalancing action even though the aggregate KPI looks healthy?
