    buffer_time_s: 0.85 -> 1.15 (Increasing inter-cycle buffer time extends the operator rest window each cycle, reducing cumulative fatigue accumulation rate. This is a complementary fix that avoids further throughput loss from cycle rate reduction — if used together with a moderate cycle rate reduction (e.g. 1.15→0.95), the additional recovery time can compensate for the remaining fatigue gap without as steep a cycle rate cut.)
    r1_speed_fraction: 0.9 -> 0.8 (Robot speed at 0.9 paces the operator indirectly — when upstream robot throughput is high, the operator must sustain elevated tempo to match the line rate, compounding fatigue beyond what the human_cycle_rate_multiplier alone captures. Reducing r1_speed_fraction to 0.80 relaxes the effective demand on the operator and also yields a small reduction in energy and noise. This is a tertiary adjustment, most useful if the human cycle rate cannot be reduced enough alone.)

